## Hydrogen
component-hydrogen = Hydrogen
    .genitive = hydrogen
component-hydrogen-description-novice = The lightest gas: 14 times lighter than air. It burns, and with air forms an explosive mixture. It is released, for example, when current passes through water.
component-hydrogen-description-school = Hydrogen has the highest specific heat of all gases (≈ 14 kJ/(kg·K)) and conducts heat very well. Burning, it forms only water.
component-hydrogen-safety-school = A hydrogen–air mixture explodes from a spark. Real experiments with hydrogen use only small amounts, away from flames.
